ured":"A multitask, multilingual, multimodal evaluation of chatgpt on reasoning, hallucination, and interactivity. (2023). Accessed. February 8, 2023: http:\/\/arXiv:2302.04023."},{"key":"ref10","unstructured":"Selfcheckgpt. zero-resource black-box hallucination detection for generative large language models. (2023). Accessed: March 15, 2023: http:\/\/arXiv:2303.08896."},{"key":"ref11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1186\/s13054-023-04473-y","article-title":"Artificial intelligence hallucinations","volume":"27","author":"Salvagno M","year":"2023","unstructured":"Salvagno M, Taccone FS, Gerli AG. Artificial intelligence hallucinations. Crit Care. 2023, 27:180. 10.1186\/s13054-023-04473-y","journal-title":"Crit Care"},{"key":"ref12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1186\/s13054-023-04425-6","article-title":"Artificial hallucination: GPT on LSD?","volume":"27","author":"Beutel G","year":"2023","unstructured":"Beutel G, Geerits E, Kielstein JT. Artificial hallucination: GPT on LSD?. Crit Care. 2023, 27:148. 10.1186\/s13054-023-04425-6","journal-title":"Crit Care"},{"key":"ref13","unstructured":"Retrieval system evaluation. (2005). Accessed. September 26, 2005: https:\/\/www.nist.gov\/publications\/retrieval-system-evaluation."},{"key":"ref14","unstructured":"LLaMA. open and efficient foundation language models. (2023). Accessed: February 27, 2023: http:\/\/arXiv:2302.13971."},{"key":"ref15","unstructured":"Raise a child in large language model. towards effective and generalizable fine-tuning. (2021). Accessed: September 13, 2021: http:\/\/arXiv:2109.05687."},{"key":"ref16","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1309\/LM6ER9WJR1IHQAUY","article-title":"A review of medical errors in laboratory diagnostics and where we are today","volume":"43","author":"Hammerling JA","year":"2012","unstructured":"Hammerling JA. A review of medical errors in laboratory diagnostics and where we are today. Laboratory Med. 2012, 43:41-4. 10.1309\/LM6ER9WJR1IHQAUY","journal-title":"Laboratory Med"},{"key":"ref17","article-title":"Benefits, limits, and risks of GPT-4 as an AI chatbot for medicine","volume":"388","author":"Lee P","year":"2023","unstructured":"Lee P, Bubeck S, Petro J. Benefits, limits, and risks of GPT-4 as an AI chatbot for medicine. New England J Med. 2023, 388:1233-9.","journal-title":"New England J Med"},{"key":"ref18","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1016\/j.dsx.2023.102744","article-title":"ChatGPT: is this version good for healthcare and research?","volume":"17","author":"Vaishya R","year":"2023","unstructured":"Vaishya R, Misra A, Vaish A. ChatGPT: is this version good for healthcare and research?. Diabet Metabol Syndr. 2023, 17:102744.","journal-title":"Diabet Metabol Syndr"},{"key":"ref19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1136\/medethics-2019-105935","article-title":"Limits of trust in medical AI","volume":"46","author":"Hatherley JJ","year":"2020","unstructured":"Hatherley JJ. Limits of trust in medical AI. J Med Ethics. 2020, 46:478-81. 10.1136\/medethics-2019-105935","journal-title":"J Med Ethics"}],"container-title":["Cureus"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cureus.com\/articles\/152858-chatdoctor-a-medical-chat-model-fine-tuned-on-a-large-language-model-meta-ai-llama-using-medical-domain-knowledge","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,9]],"date-time":"2024-02-09T14:51:41Z","timestamp":1707490301000},"score":37.858963,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cureus.com\/articles\/152858-chatdoctor-a-medical-chat-model-fine-tuned-on-a-large-language-model-meta-ai-llama-using-medical-domain-knowledge"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,6,24]]},"references-count":19,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7759\/cureus.40895","ISSN":["2168-8184"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2168-8184","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2023,6,24]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,13]],"date-time":"2026-05-13T13:32:32Z","timestamp":1778679152029,"version":"3.51.4"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2023,8,8]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Wiley","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Recently, Large-scale Language Models (LLMs) such as Chat Generative\nPre-trained Transformer (ChatGPT) and Generative Pre-trained Transformer\n4 (GPT-4) have demonstrated remarkable performance in the general\ndomain. However, Inadaptability in a particular domain have led to\nhallucination for these LLMs when responding in specific domain\ncontexts. The issue has attracted widespread attention, existing\ndomain-centered fine-tuning efforts have predominantly focused on\nsectors like medical, financial, and legal, leaving critical areas such\nas power energy relatively unexplored. To bridge this gap, this paper\nintroduces a novel power energy chat model called PowerPulse. Built upon\nthe open and efficient foundation language models (LLaMA) architecture,\nPowerPulse is fine-tuned specifically on Chinese Power Sector Domain\nKnowledge. This work marks the inaugural application of the LLaMA model\nin the field of power energy. By leveraging pertinent pre-training data\nand instruction fine-tuning datasets tailored for the power energy\ndomain, the PowerPulse model showcases exceptional performance in tasks\nsuch as text generation, summary extraction, and topic classification.\nExperimental results validate the efficacy of the PowerPulse model,\nmaking significant contributions to the advancement of specialized\nlanguage models in specific domains.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.22541\/au.169152136.62259950\/v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,8,8]],"date-time":"2023-08-08T15:02:47Z","timestamp":1691506967000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["PowerPulse: Power Energy Chat Model with LLaMA Model Fine-tuned on Chinese and Power Sector Domain Knowledge"],"prefix":"10.22541","author":[{"given":"qiong","family":"nong","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"ChunLin","family":"Yin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan Power Grid Co Ltd"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"KunPeng","family":"Du","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"HongCheng","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan Power Grid Co Ltd"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Li","family":"Yang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan Power Grid Co Ltd"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Bin","family":"Yan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan Power Grid Co Ltd"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Huang","family":"Xiang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan Power Grid Co Ltd"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"XiaoBo","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2929-2126","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xuan","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Yunnan University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"311","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.authorea.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.22541\/au.169152136.62259950\/v1","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,13]],"date-time":"2026-05-13T12:49:57Z","timestamp":1778676597000},"score":37.47396,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.authorea.com\/doi\/full\/10.22541\/au.169152136.62259950\/v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,8,8]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.22541\/au.169152136.62259950\/v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2023,8,8]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"institution":[{"name":"San Jose State University","acronym":["SJSU","SJSU"],"place":["San Jose, CA, USA"],"department":["Applied Data Science"]}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,31]],"date-time":"2026-07-31T15:59:03Z","timestamp":1785513543424,"version":"3.56.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"San Jose State University Library","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.31979\/etd.54rk-euuc","type":"dissertation","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,31]],"date-time":"2026-07-31T15:10:19Z","timestamp":1785510619000},"approved":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,27]]},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Explainable Deepfake Audio Detection Using Fine-Tuned Foundation Models"],"prefix":"10.31979","author":[{"given":"Janani Kripa","family":"Manoharan","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"San Jose State University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"16862","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/scholarworks.sjsu.edu\/cgi\/viewcontent.cgi?article=9312&amp;context=etd_theses&amp;unstamped=1","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,31]],"date-time":"2026-07-31T15:10:51Z","timestamp":1785510651000},"score":37.24524,"degree":["Master of Science (MS)"],"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/scholarworks.sjsu.edu\/etd_theses\/5764"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.31979\/etd.54rk-euuc"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,27]],"date-time":"2026-10-27T13:34:43Z","timestamp":1793108083342,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":35,"publisher":"MDPI AG","issue":"11","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,24]],"date-time":"2026-10-24T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1792800000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,24]],"date-time":"2026-10-24T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1792800000000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Algorithms"],"abstract":"<jats:p>The growing prevalence of mental health disorders, combined with limited access to traditional therapeutic services, has accelerated the demand for scalable and empathetic AI-based interventions. This study explores the development and evaluation of an AI-powered chatbot designed to provide mental health support using advanced Large Language Models (LLMs), specifically LLaMA 2 and LLaMA 3. Using a mental health counseling dataset, the models were fine-tuned on counseling context\u2013response pairs and evaluated for semantic and lexical similarity to reference responses. The training pipeline incorporated quantization, LoRA adaptation and a structured prompt template. The models were evaluated using BERTScore, BLEU, ROUGE, and METEOR, offering a multi-dimensional view of linguistic and semantic quality. Results show that LLaMA 3 achieved a higher mean BERTScore F1 than LLaMA 2 (0.860 versus 0.835). The results characterize the fine-tuned models\u2019 performance under automatic text-similarity evaluation. Human evaluation is required before conclusions can be drawn about empathy, safety or suitability for mental health support. Ethical considerations and future directions, including user validation and multimodal expansion, are also discussed.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3390\/a19110913","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,27]],"date-time":"2026-10-27T12:07:58Z","timestamp":1793102878000},"page":"913","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/mdpi_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Enhancing Mental Health Support Using Fine-Tuned Large Language Models: A Comparative Evaluation of LLaMA 2 and LLaMA 3"],"prefix":"10.3390","volume":"19","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3668-6230","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Essa Q.","family":"Shahra","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Architecture, Built Environment, Computing and Engineering (ABCE), Birmingham City University, STEAMhouse, Belmont Row, Birmingham B4 7RQ, UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"},{"role":"conceptualization","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"formal-analysis","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-original-draft","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"project-administration","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"funding-acquisition","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-review-editing","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"investigation","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"methodology","vocabulary":"credit"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0800-428X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Rasheed","family":"Mohammad","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Architecture, Built Environment, Computing and Engineering (ABCE), Birmingham City University, STEAMhouse, Belmont Row, Birmingham B4 7RQ, UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"},{"role":"project-administration","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-original-draft","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"formal-analysis","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"conceptualization","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"methodology","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"investigation","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-review-editing","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"funding-acquisition","vocabulary":"credit"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5164-8403","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Waheb A.","family":"Jabbar","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Architecture, Built Environment, Computing and Engineering (ABCE), Birmingham City University, STEAMhouse, Belmont Row, Birmingham B4 7RQ, UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"},{"role":"conceptualization","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"formal-analysis","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-original-draft","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"funding-acquisition","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-review-editing","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"investigation","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"methodology","vocabulary":"credit"}]}],"member":"1968","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,24]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref_1","unstructured":"World Health Organization (2022). World Mental Health Report: Transforming Mental Health for All, World Health Organization."},{"key":"ref_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"57","DOI":"10.1007\/s10728-025-00549-8","article-title":"Transforming public mental health: A review on global trends, challenges, and pathways to change","volume":"34","author":"Okesanya","year":"2026","journal-title":"Health Care Anal."},{"key":"ref_3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"61","DOI":"10.1192\/S2056474000001240","article-title":"Brain drain: A challenge to global mental health","volume":"13","author":"Oladeji","year":"2016","journal-title":"BJPsych Int."},{"key":"ref_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Khatri, R.B., and Assefa, Y. (2022). Access to health services among culturally and linguistically diverse populations in the Australian universal health care system: Issues and challenges. BMC Public Health, 22.","DOI":"10.1186\/s12889-022-13256-z"},{"key":"ref_5","unstructured":"World Health Organization (2024). Community-Based Mental Health Services in the WHO South-East Asia Region, World Health Organization."},{"key":"ref_6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"137","DOI":"10.1016\/S2215-0366(21)00395-3","article-title":"Global, regional, and national burden of 12 mental disorders in 204 countries and territories, 1990\u20132019: A systematic analysis for the Global Burden of Disease Study 2019","volume":"9","author":"Ferrari","year":"2022","journal-title":"Lancet Psychiatry"},{"key":"ref_7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","f